    <a class="press-item" id="leo" href="/conferences/"><img src="/images/emblem-holy-see.svg" alt="" style="max-height:64px"><div><h3>The medal of Pope Leo XIV's first year</h3><p class="meta">Presented by Archbishop Gabriele Caccia, Apostolic Nuncio to the United States · Washington, July 14, 2026</p><p>Sent by the Holy Father to the founder of the Orientale Lumen Conferences on the occasion of the thirtieth. The medal commemorates the 1700th anniversary of the Council of Nicaea and bears Christ's prayer <em>ut mundus credat</em>, that the world may believe.</p></div></a>
    <a class="press-item" id="koch" href="/conferences/"><img src="/images/emblem-holy-see.svg" alt="" style="max-height:64px"><div><h3>Address of Cardinal Kurt Koch to Orientale Lumen XXX</h3><p class="meta">Prefect, Dicastery for Promoting Christian Unity · Rome, July 15, 2026</p><p>"Becoming a common heritage could be the definition of reception. In a sense, this Orientale Lumen Conference is also part of this reception process."</p></div></a>
